        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Pearcy, Alexander O'Neal, Al Pitrelli, Hiro Kuretani\n- Bands: Ratt, Vertex, Arcade, Vicious Delite, Nitronic, Danger Danger, Hotshot, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, Trans-Siberian Orchestra, WXXI, Trancentral Station\n- Roles: musician, singer, songwriter, arranger, guitarist, drummer, founder\n- Places: Natchez, Mississippi\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander O'Neal was born on November 15, 1953.\n- Alexander O'Neal is an American R&B singer, songwriter, and arranger from Natchez, Mississippi.\n- Stephen Pearcy was born on July 3, 1956.\n- Stephen Pearcy is an American musician.\n- Stephen Pearcy is best known as the founder, singer, and songwriter of the heavy metal band Ratt.\n- Vertex was formed in 1995.\n- Vertex featured singer Stephen Pearcy, who was associated with Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, and Nitronic.\n- Vertex featured guitarist Al Pitrelli, who was associated with Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, and Trans-Siberian Orchestra.\n- Vertex featured drummer Hiro Kuretani, who was associated with WXXI and Trancentral Station.",
